# Contact form delivery. The key is minted through Atlas (client > Documentation
# > API > Resend tab), which is why it is named ATLAS_API_KEY here. It must be a
# Resend key (re_...) — the route talks to Resend. RESEND_API_KEY also works as
# a fallback name. Without either, the form still accepts submissions but emails
# nothing (logged to the console in dev).
ATLAS_API_KEY=

# Verified sender on capitalhoardings.com.au once the domain is added to Resend.
CONTACT_FROM="Capital Hoardings Website <no-reply@capitalhoardings.com.au>"

# Where enquiries are delivered. Defaults to office@capitalhoardings.com.au.
CONTACT_TO=office@capitalhoardings.com.au

# Cloudflare Turnstile (optional). The API only enforces the check once
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is set, so the form keeps working until you configure it.
# Server-side verification only for now — adding the widget to the form would
# also need NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY and a change to ContactForm.tsx.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
